<title>UK: Demand lower at London tea auction.</title>
<headline>Demand lower at London tea auction.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Demand was down at the London tea auction on Monday, the offical report said.</p>
<p>Among the landeds, top quality Assams saw keen competition but prices for bright liquoring Kenyas were down.</p>
<p>Coloury medium prices tended higher and Brightest Burundis also sold well.</p>
<p>But prices were generally 3-6 pence per kg easier and there were some withdrawals.</p>
<p>Offshore teas saw good demand at higher prices with 1,200 packages on offer.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
